#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Antigravity CLI's (agy's) stand-in, for the smoke suite and the sandbox: it does what the VM run of
2026-11-11 showed the real agy 1.5.5 doing (the captures and payloads are in tests/fixtures/agy/) and nothing
it was not seen to do. It has no login, no network and no model: its "model" is a script, read from the
prompt.

Commands, into its own ~/.gemini:
  --version                       1.5.5
  models                          model names
  mcp list                        the servers of config/mcp_config.json, or "No MCP servers configured."
  plugin install <dir>            copies the plugin to config/plugins/<name>/ and writes
                                  config/import_manifest.json
  plugin uninstall <name>         removes it, and leaves import_manifest.json (its imports null) and an empty
                                  antigravity-cli/plugin_data/<name>/, as the real one does
  plugin list [--json]            the plugins
Anything else is a session in the pane, drawn as the screens of tests/fixtures/agy/screens/ are: a box (the
`>` line between two grey rules), `? for shortcuts` under it when idle, `esc to cancel` and a spinner when a
turn runs, a dialog ("Run this command?", numbered options) for a command named ask, and text typed or
pasted into the box (bracketed paste, as `bosun send` pastes) with the hint blanked. Flags:
--prompt-interactive (a first prompt), --conversation <id> (an unknown id prints `warning: conversation
"<id>" not found` and starts a fresh conversation), --settings <json> (a key other than agentMode and
trustedWorkspaces is an error, as `hooks` is for agy), --log-file, --model, --effort, --remote-control.
A conversation is antigravity-cli/conversations/<id>.db (written at its first prompt), with
presence/<id>.lock while open.

It runs the hooks of the installed plugins (config/plugins/*/hooks.json) as agy does: each handler through
`sh -c` in the plugin's folder, with this process's environment and the payload on stdin. SessionStart at a
new conversation's first prompt (never on a resume), PreInvocation before each model call, PreToolUse before a
run_command (handlers grouped under a `matcher`), Stop at the end of a turn, with fullyIdle false while a
background task runs. A handler's answer: nothing is no opinion; {"decision":"auto_approve",...} approves;
anything else, a blank decision, {} and an exit other than 0 refuse the tool; a PreInvocation answer with
terminationBehavior terminate stops the turn before its model call, saying the step's userMessage. Esc
cancels a turn and fires no hook.

What the scripted model does with a prompt, first match first:
  run <command>   a run_command tool call for <command> (to the end of the line): PreToolUse, then the command
                  runs unless a hook refused it, then a second model call
  ask             a run_command for a command named ask: PreToolUse, then, if no hook answered, the dialog,
                  which Enter, 1, 2 or 3 answer yes, and 4 or Esc cancel the turn
  sleep <n>       a turn that takes n seconds (Esc cancels it)
  background [n]  the turn ends at once, Stop with fullyIdle false, and n seconds later (3 without one) a turn
                  of its own starts, with the same lastUserInput, and ends fully idle
  anything else   one line, "[stand-in] ok"
The word `/exit` leaves, as agy's does.

ps names a script's process for its interpreter, and bosun finds an agy by the name of its command's first
word, so a session starts again as `bash -c` under this file's own name, which runs the program as its child.
"""

